        "content": "<p>Usually <code>logInfo</code> inside <code>run_meta</code> blocks log at the <code>run_meta</code> token. That can be inconvenient or not just right when the <code>run_meta</code> block gets longer. The following trick works:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ToExpr</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tk</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"s2\">\"here\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">toExpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tk</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">run_meta</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- ... several lines</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">withRef</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">here</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- at `here` it is logged</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"Log1\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"Log2\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- ... several lines</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I wonder whether there already is something like that built into Lean. Ideally something like a <code>with_ref_here</code> that collapses the <code>withRef here do</code> in the above code and sets the <code>with_ref_here</code>token as the ref. (I briefly tried to come up with a solution myself, but ran into problems, e.g., a missing instance for <code>Quote Syntax</code> when trying to implement it as a macro.)</p>",
        "id": 596445975,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Miele",
        "timestamp": 1779282285
    },
